  "narrative": {
    "summaryIntro": "Kalighat Temple in Kolkata is one of the 51 Shakti Pithas and is dedicated to Goddess Kali, the fierce form of the divine mother. Located on the banks of the Hooghly River, the temple holds immense spiritual significance in Tantra and Shakta traditions. According to legend, the toes of the goddess fell at this location when Shiva performed his cosmic dance with the goddess's lifeless body.\n\nThe temple is one of the oldest and most important religious sites in Kolkata and has been a center of devotion for centuries. The current structure was rebuilt in 1809 and features distinctive Bengali architectural style. The temple remains a vibrant place of worship and has served as an inspiration to spiritual leaders and reformers throughout history, including Ramakrishna Paramahamsa.",
